BT 1 0 0 1 0 48 Tm -0.036818 Tw 11.4 TL /F3 9 Tf .133333 .192157 .227451 rg (Abstract -) Tj /F4 9 Tf ( A naive random lunch generator can repeat the same dish, overuse a food family, or recommend an explicitly rejected item. I) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.085154 Tw (extended a no-build HTML/CSS/JavaScript baseline with cluster-aware filtering, a three-recommendation cooldown, a session blacklist,) Tj T* 0 Tw .636188 Tw (balanced catalog coverage, valid icons, and low-inventory feedback. The final deterministic regression suite passed ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (13/13 tests) Tj /F4 9 Tf (; three) Tj T* 0 Tw .7245 Tw (separate 100,000-selection checks reported zero identical-adjacent, same-cluster-adjacent, and cooldown violations while reaching all) Tj T* 0 Tw (42 dishes. The result shows that small, explicit candidate filters can substantially improve variety and user control without a backend.) Tj T* ET
